<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Umm al-Quwain</h1><p class="st-meta">1775 CE – 1971 CE (approx.) · capital Umm al-Quwain</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The small Al Mualla sheikhdom on the Trucial Coast, one of the founding members of the United Arab Emirates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ali">Al Ali</a> tribe, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mualla">Al Mualla</a> family, founded a fortified settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umm-al-quwain">Umm al-Quwain</a> on a sandy peninsula of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial Coast</a> in 1775 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-majid-al-mualla">Rashid bin Majid Al Mualla</a>. It also held the inland oasis of Falaj al-Mualla.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sheikhdom lived from fishing, pearling and boatbuilding, with the lagoon and its mangroves at its centre. It signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a> and became one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a> under British protection. It was among the poorest of the sheikhdoms, without significant oil, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-bin-rashid-al-mualla">Ahmad bin Rashid Al Mualla</a> ruled it from 1929 to 1981.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umm-al-quwain">Umm al-Quwain</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> at its foundation in December 1971 and remains one of its seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-umm-al-quwain.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Umm al-Quwain" width="320" height="222"><figcaption>Image: Peter Dowley from Dubai, United Arab Emirates · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umm_Al_Quwain_mangroves_(7267363924).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1775 CE – 1971 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Umm al-Quwain</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rashid bin Majid Al Mualla, Ahmad bin Rashid Al Mualla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Umm al-Quwain, Emirate of Umm al-Quwain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1873&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-umm-al-quwain" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Umm al-Quwain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6151 1238 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Umm al-Quwain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6471 1494L6439 1557M6471 1494L6446 1533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6439 1557h0M6446 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6471 1494h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6471 1494h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1873&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-umm-al-quwain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
